Basic Rules
General Information

All API requests must be made over HTTPS and are only supported via the POST method.
Data Format

    Standard Requests: Use JSON as the data interchange format for the message body. Set the HTTP header as follows:

Content-Type: application/json

    File/Image Upload Requests: Use the MULTIPART data format. Set the HTTP header as follows:

Content-Type: multipart/form-data

Character Encoding

All API requests and responses must use UTF-8 encoding
Date Format

All date fields are currently based on China Standard Time (GMT+8) and use the following format:yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss
Request Unique Identifier

The platform will assign a unique identifier to each received request. This identifier is included in the response HTTP header J-Trace-ID. If you need any support, please provide this identifier to help us locate the specific request quickly.
Error Information

HTTP Status Codes

    200: The platform has received the request and returned a response. This does not indicate business-level success; check the response body for business-specific result codes.
    400: Invalid request parameters, typically related to authentication or validation.
    401: Unauthorized request. Usually due to signature verification failure.
    403: Forbidden. The request is not allowed.
    500: Internal server error on the open platform.

Error Codes and Messages

When a request fails at the business level, the API returns an error response in the body in the following format:

    code: Detailed error code.
    message: Human-readable description of the error cause.

Example:  

{
  "code": 1001,
  "message": "Insufficient prepaid balance"
}

